# CLAUDE.md: house rules for this project

Claude reads this file at the start of every session in this folder.
Put the global parts (security, quality failure protocol, memory) in ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md so they apply everywhere.
Delete anything that does not fit your project. Short and true beats long and ignored.

---

## Security: non-negotiable

### Before ANY commit or push
```bash
./scripts/security-check.sh   # must pass. Never skip it.
```
If a repo has no `security-check.sh`, say so out loud and do a manual pass (search for keys and tokens, confirm `.env` is ignored) before committing. Never skip silently.

### Safe versions
These were the minimum safe versions when this template was written (March 2026).
**Versions go stale. Check the current security advisories before you rely on this table.**

| Thing | Minimum safe | Note |
|---|---|---|
| React | 19.0.4+ / 19.1.5+ / 19.2.4+ | earlier patches of each line are incomplete |
| Next.js | 16.0.7+ or 15.5.7+ | |
| Node.js | 24.13.0+ or 22.20.0+ | Node 20 is end of life, do not use it |

### Secrets
- No keys, tokens or passwords in code, ever. They live in `.env` files that git ignores, or in your host's secret settings.
- Example config files hold placeholders only (`YOUR_KEY_HERE`).
- A key that was ever committed is a leaked key. Rotate it, then remove it.

