## Forbidden anti-patterns

```javascript
try { ... } catch (e) {}     // empty catch: the error vanishes. FORBIDDEN
fetch(url)                   // unhandled promise: no await, no .catch. FORBIDDEN
const KEY = "abc123"         // hardcoded secret. FORBIDDEN
```

```bash
git push   # without running ./scripts/security-check.sh first. FORBIDDEN
```

Also: no `console.log` left in app code, no "temporary" code without a comment saying when it goes.

---

## Script naming

| Use | Never use |
|---|---|
| `start-app.sh` | `run.sh` |
| `stop-app.sh` | `server.sh` |
| `setup.sh` | `launch.sh` |
| `dev.sh` | `init.sh` |
| `security-check.sh` | anything else for security |
| `verify-quality.sh` | anything else for quality |

Predictable names mean anyone (and any agent) can find the right script without asking.

